<Base title="Writing a Fudge plugin (planned)" description="The planned JSON-over-stdio plugin protocol for Fudge Launcher, with a Python example. Planned for v0.3.">
  <div class="page"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h1>Plugins <span class="planned">planned for v0.3</span></h1>
    <p class="status"><strong>This is a design, not a shipped feature.</strong> Fudge is pre-alpha and the plugin host does not exist yet. The protocol below follows the project plan and may change before v0.3. Nothing here can be run today.</p>

    <h2>The idea</h2>
    <p>A plugin is a program, in any language, that talks JSON over stdin and stdout. Fudge's own built-in features use the same provider interface internally, so external plugins are meant to be first-class.</p>

    <h2>Layout</h2>
    <p>Each plugin lives in its own folder with a manifest:</p>
<pre><code>~/.local/share/fudge/plugins/&lt;id&gt;/plugin.toml</code></pre>
    <p>The manifest holds the plugin's <code>id</code>, the <code>keyword</code> that triggers it, the <code>exec</code> command to start it, and its <code>version</code>.</p>
<pre><code>id      = "hello"
keyword = "hi"
exec    = "python3 plugin.py"
version = "0.1.0"</code></pre>

    <h2>The protocol</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Fudge starts your program the first time its keyword is typed and keeps it running.</li>
      <li>For each query it writes one JSON message per line to your stdin, such as <code>{`{"method":"query","params":{"text":"hi bob"}}`}</code>.</li>
      <li>You reply with one JSON line containing a list of results. Each result has a title, a subtitle and an action. Actions in the plan are <code>open</code>, <code>copy</code>, <code>run</code> and <code>paste</code>.</li>
      <li>The host applies timeouts, so slow plugins cannot freeze the box.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The exact field names for replies are not final. The example uses a plausible shape.</p>

    <h2>A 20-line Python plugin <span class="planned">planned for v0.3</span></h2>
<pre><code>#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Draft example: replies "Hello, NAME" and copies it on Enter.
import json, sys

for line in sys.stdin:
    msg = json.loads(line)
    if msg.get("method") != "query":
        continue
    text = msg["params"]["text"].strip()
    name = text.removeprefix("hi").strip() or "world"
    reply = &#123;
        "results": [&#123;
            "title": f"Hello, &#123;name&#125;!",
            "subtitle": "Press Enter to copy",
            "action": &#123;"type": "copy", "text": f"Hello, &#123;name&#125;!"&#125;,
        &#125;]
    &#125;
    print(json.dumps(reply), flush=True)</code></pre>

    <h2>Registry <span class="planned">planned</span></h2>
    <p>The plan is a git-backed registry: a GitHub repository with an <code>index.json</code> signed with minisign, verified by the app before anything is installed. Plugin downloads happen only when you browse or install, as listed in the <a href="../privacy/">privacy page</a>.</p>
  </div></div>
</Base>
